WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:06.308
Here is the exam graph from part one

2
00:00:06.308 --> 00:00:09.900
six exams, and a line for every clash.

3
00:00:10.250 --> 00:00:13.631
Exams in the same time slot must not clash.

4
00:00:13.709 --> 00:00:16.225
What is the largest set of exams

5
00:00:16.304 --> 00:00:18.191
that can share one slot?

6
00:00:18.191 --> 00:00:19.763
Could four of them?

7
00:00:19.763 --> 00:00:21.650
Pause and look for one.

8
00:00:25.230 --> 00:00:27.926
First, graphs inside graphs.

9
00:00:28.022 --> 00:00:31.681
H is a subgraph of G when its vertices

10
00:00:31.777 --> 00:00:34.666
are some of the vertices of G

11
00:00:34.666 --> 00:00:38.710
and its edges are some of the edges of G.

12
00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:43.455
For example, keep only b, c, d and e

13
00:00:43.455 --> 00:00:47.731
and only the two edges b c and d e.

14
00:00:47.731 --> 00:00:50.700
That is a subgraph of G.

15
00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:56.698
A spanning subgraph keeps every vertex.

16
00:00:56.698 --> 00:01:02.671
Keep all six exams, but only five clashes

17
00:01:02.671 --> 00:01:06.560
a b, b d, c d, c e and e f.

18
00:01:06.910 --> 00:01:09.273
It spans the whole graph

19
00:01:09.273 --> 00:01:12.392
but some edges of G are missing

20
00:01:12.392 --> 00:01:13.620
such as a c.

21
00:01:13.620 --> 00:01:17.590
So it is spanning, but it is not induced.

22
00:01:18.170 --> 00:01:23.253
An induced subgraph is chosen the other way.

23
00:01:23.253 --> 00:01:27.990
Choose some vertices, say b, c, d and e

24
00:01:27.990 --> 00:01:33.073
and keep every edge of G between them: b c

25
00:01:33.073 --> 00:01:35.730
b d, c d, c e and d e.

26
00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:37.827
Nothing is left out

27
00:01:37.915 --> 00:01:40.797
so for each set of vertices there

28
00:01:40.885 --> 00:01:43.680
is exactly one induced subgraph.

29
00:01:44.260 --> 00:01:47.576
Now compare the first example: b, c

30
00:01:47.576 --> 00:01:50.523
d and e, with only b c and d e.

31
00:01:50.523 --> 00:01:53.747
It has the same vertices, but b d

32
00:01:53.747 --> 00:01:56.050
c d and c e are missing.

33
00:01:56.050 --> 00:01:57.984
So it is a subgraph

34
00:01:57.984 --> 00:02:01.300
but it is not the induced subgraph.

35
00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:04.841
A clique is a set of vertices that

36
00:02:04.928 --> 00:02:07.627
are all adjacent to each other.

37
00:02:07.627 --> 00:02:09.891
a, b and c form a clique

38
00:02:09.891 --> 00:02:13.200
three exams that clash in every pair.

39
00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:16.160
So do b, c and d, and c, d and e.

40
00:02:16.510 --> 00:02:19.350
The clique number, omega of G

41
00:02:19.350 --> 00:02:22.474
is the size of a largest clique.

42
00:02:22.474 --> 00:02:25.030
Is there a clique of four?

43
00:02:25.380 --> 00:02:27.092
In a clique of four

44
00:02:27.092 --> 00:02:30.858
each vertex has three neighbours inside it

45
00:02:30.858 --> 00:02:33.682
so its degree is at least three.

46
00:02:33.682 --> 00:02:34.624
Only b, c

47
00:02:34.624 --> 00:02:37.619
d and e have degree three or more

48
00:02:37.619 --> 00:02:40.187
and b and e are not adjacent.

49
00:02:40.187 --> 00:02:42.840
So there is no clique of four

50
00:02:42.840 --> 00:02:44.980
and omega of G is three.

51
00:02:45.560 --> 00:02:48.547
An independent set is the opposite

52
00:02:48.547 --> 00:02:51.705
no two of its vertices are adjacent.

53
00:02:51.705 --> 00:02:53.497
a, d and f, algebra

54
00:02:53.497 --> 00:02:55.631
data science and French

55
00:02:55.631 --> 00:02:57.679
have no clashes at all

56
00:02:57.679 --> 00:02:59.898
so they can share a slot.

57
00:02:59.898 --> 00:03:03.056
Alpha of G, the independence number

58
00:03:03.056 --> 00:03:06.640
is the size of a largest independent set.

59
00:03:06.990 --> 00:03:09.296
Proving that alpha of G is

60
00:03:09.385 --> 00:03:11.424
three takes two halves.

61
00:03:11.424 --> 00:03:14.351
First, an example of size three

62
00:03:14.351 --> 00:03:15.504
we have one.

63
00:03:15.504 --> 00:03:18.696
Second, a reason why no independent

64
00:03:18.785 --> 00:03:20.470
set of four exists.

65
00:03:20.820 --> 00:03:23.154
Take any independent set S.

66
00:03:23.154 --> 00:03:26.697
If S contains c, it contains none of the

67
00:03:26.784 --> 00:03:28.598
four neighbours of c

68
00:03:28.598 --> 00:03:30.846
so S sits inside c and f

69
00:03:30.846 --> 00:03:33.438
and has at most two vertices.

70
00:03:33.438 --> 00:03:35.599
If S does not contain c

71
00:03:35.685 --> 00:03:38.192
split the other five vertices

72
00:03:38.278 --> 00:03:41.822
into three groups: a b, d e, and f alone.

73
00:03:41.822 --> 00:03:44.587
The first two groups are edges

74
00:03:44.674 --> 00:03:47.180
so S takes at most one vertex

75
00:03:47.267 --> 00:03:48.649
from each group

76
00:03:48.649 --> 00:03:52.020
and has at most three vertices in all.

77
00:03:52.370 --> 00:03:54.638
So alpha of G is three.

78
00:03:54.638 --> 00:03:58.090
Four exams can never share a slot.

79
00:03:58.670 --> 00:03:59.555
A warning.

80
00:03:59.555 --> 00:04:02.477
c and f form an independent set

81
00:04:02.477 --> 00:04:05.309
and nothing can be added to it

82
00:04:05.309 --> 00:04:08.231
every other vertex is next to c

83
00:04:08.231 --> 00:04:09.470
or next to f.

84
00:04:09.820 --> 00:04:13.534
So it is stuck, but it is not the largest.

85
00:04:13.534 --> 00:04:16.010
It is maximal, not maximum.

86
00:04:16.099 --> 00:04:18.486
The largest independent set

87
00:04:18.575 --> 00:04:20.255
has three vertices

88
00:04:20.344 --> 00:04:23.262
and a greedy search that stops as

89
00:04:23.350 --> 00:04:26.180
soon as it is stuck can miss it.

90
00:04:26.760 --> 00:04:28.751
Now the timetable.

91
00:04:28.751 --> 00:04:31.184
Slot one: a, d and f.

92
00:04:31.184 --> 00:04:33.285
Slot two: b and e.

93
00:04:33.285 --> 00:04:36.160
Slot three: c on its own.

94
00:04:36.160 --> 00:04:39.920
Every slot is an independent set.

95
00:04:40.270 --> 00:04:42.636
Could two slots be enough?

96
00:04:42.636 --> 00:04:43.000
No.

97
00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:45.365
a, b and c form a clique

98
00:04:45.365 --> 00:04:48.367
three exams that clash in pairs

99
00:04:48.367 --> 00:04:51.643
so they need three different slots.

100
00:04:51.643 --> 00:04:54.190
Three slots is the minimum.

101
00:04:54.770 --> 00:04:55.592
To sum up.

102
00:04:55.674 --> 00:04:58.715
A subgraph keeps some of the vertices

103
00:04:58.797 --> 00:05:00.605
and some of the edges.

104
00:05:00.605 --> 00:05:03.893
A spanning subgraph keeps every vertex

105
00:05:03.975 --> 00:05:07.262
and an induced subgraph keeps every edge

106
00:05:07.345 --> 00:05:09.810
between the vertices it chose.

107
00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:13.183
Omega is the size of a largest clique

108
00:05:13.183 --> 00:05:16.762
alpha the size of a largest independent set

109
00:05:16.762 --> 00:05:20.024
and proving either one takes two halves

110
00:05:20.024 --> 00:05:20.978
an example

111
00:05:20.978 --> 00:05:24.160
and a reason why nothing larger exists.

112
00:05:24.510 --> 00:05:25.330
Try this

113
00:05:25.421 --> 00:05:28.790
the five-cycle has no clique of three

114
00:05:28.881 --> 00:05:31.795
and no independent set of three.

115
00:05:31.886 --> 00:05:35.347
Prove that every graph on six vertices

116
00:05:35.438 --> 00:05:37.350
has one or the other.
